  "key": "AIN-161",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Packages] Remove local dependency overrides and consume registry artifacts",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User request: remove all local package overrides. Consumers must resolve declared versioned registry packages rather than sibling source/builds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scope: API Docker linking/build setup; frontend bind mounts and aliases; local XDS dependency declarations/locks; staging scripts; installed sibling links and copied private-package artifacts; regression checks and documentation. Inspect existing vendored Services client separately: do not invent a registry package or silently replace its contract."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acceptance: no private dependency resolves to a sibling checkout through configuration, installation links, or injected dist; Docker installs from consumer locks without source linking; supported clean registry install and runtime provenance checks fail explicitly on missing/old releases; preserve application data and record any authentication/publication blockers. Remove legacy staging command. No new user workflow, so package provenance and configuration integration evidence replaces UI stories."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "AIN-13 remains related release parity work and is not replaced or closed. Parent AIN-1 and related AIN-55 broader CI/database requirements remain outside this bounded removal. No publication or production deployment is requested."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "parent": {
